From 3690cab8bcc9e5f2b658d0e736f71277a49abdbe Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maximilian Khan <maxjkh@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 14 Aug 2026 12:45:07 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] beast-rank: low-rank VRAM research kernels + gradmatrix tool
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Local research instrumentation for the beast-rank campaign, developed
2026-08-03/04 against b10066-188-g0ef6e55ed and never committed until now.

CUDA / ggml:
  ggml-cuda/mmvq.cu       +267  low-rank correction path in the MMVQ kernels
  ggml-cuda/quantize.cu   +180  re-rounding / quantize-side support
  ggml-cuda/ggml-cuda.cu  +138  dispatch + wiring
  ggml-cuda/common.cuh     +27
  ggml-alloc.c             +60
  ggml.c / ggml.h          +41  op plumbing
  ggml-cpu/*                +3  CPU fallbacks

llama:
  llama-graph.cpp          +40  graph-level correction hookup
  llama-context.cpp         +7

tooling:
  tools/imatrix/imatrix.cpp +205  gradient/covariance capture for the campaign
  tools/gradmatrix/          NEW  422-line standalone gradmatrix extractor

Measured result of this work: +79% on the 0.6B kernel trilogy (see the
openbeast repo, research/lowrank/ — MASTER-TABLE.md and RESULTS_ROLLUP.md).

Committed as a rescue point before rebasing onto current upstream master
(we are 180 commits behind; 9 of these 14 files also changed upstream).
A patch export of this commit is vendored in the openbeast repo at
research/lowrank/kernels/, which survives a re-clone of this directory —
llama.cpp/ is gitignored by the parent repo and is NOT captured by it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
